# Citroën 2CV six-light saloon, 1948-1990.
#
# The "deux chevaux": 3,860 mm long, 1,480 mm wide, 1,600 mm high, 2,400 mm
# wheelbase; 375-602 cc air-cooled flat twin, front-wheel drive, canvas roof and
# removable seats. Built until 1990, the archetypal cheap car of the 1950s-80s.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citro%C3%ABn_2CV
#
# Colours: Grey, Blue, Red and Green are documented 2CV colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 180 in total (grey 55, blue 50, red 40, green 35).
#
# Speed 100 km/h; comfort 45/398 (line). Classes 1,2.
# Dates: 1948-1990 with a road tail to about 2000.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/citroen-2cv.blend. References:
# citycars/references/citroen-2cv/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=Citroen2CV(Grey)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=55
intro_year=1948
intro_month=10
retire_year=2000
retire_month=6
speed=100
length=2
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=45
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=398

